Independently written local interoperability client, CLI/MCP transports,
capability policies and tests. Interface names and parameter structures
are used for compatibility with AirJelly's local Public API.

AirJelly is a third-party application governed by its own license. Its
implementation, binaries, recordings and credentials are not distributed
here. This is not an official vendor plugin and does not bypass licensing.
Generated repository artwork illustrates the API workflow, not recorded data.
